{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-skein-mass-relation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:skein-mass-relation","kind":"remark","title":"$q$-Deformed Skein Relation (Observation)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-skein-decomposition","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-weight-decomposition-exists","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-categorical-reeb-exists","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-substrate-parameter-exists"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-topological-mass-formula","tags":["mass","skein"],"text":"skein-mass-relation.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:skein-mass-relation\"></a><p>The mass functional <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}(\\mathfrak{H})</code> obeys the quantum Skein relation:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">q \\mathfrak{m}(L_+) - q^{-1}\\mathfrak{m}(L_-) = (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})\\mathfrak{m}(L_0).</code></pre>\n<p>Evaluating the lepton mass ratio <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_{\\mu}/m_{e}</code> determines the local substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\frac{m_{\\mu}}{m_{e}} \\;\\stackrel{\\text{LO}}{=}\\; \\frac{\\mathrm{Vol}(4_1)}{\\hbar_q^2}\n  \\approx \\frac{2.02988}{(1 - q^{-1})^2},\n\\qquad 206.7683 \\implies q \\approx 1.10998.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"16.4.3"}
